  "TourPoints": [
    {
      "Id": "b7ef0638-eddb-4ef7-b086-724ac8b32cae",
      "Description": "Continuing from the previous example, you might wonder why TiXL uses this approach.\nIt may sound less efficient at first, and in some cases it is."
    },
    {
      "Id": "25fc897a-2904-4f60-afe8-f2bb0fbbaeef",
      "Description": "However, this is a deliberate trade-off that is faster in most real-world scenarios.\nGraphics cards struggle with drawing many small objects, where “small” means very few polygons.\nIt is much faster to draw a single object with millions of faces than to draw a thousand cubes with twelve faces each."
    },
    {
      "Id": "6c0c731b-337c-41eb-8c7e-4cb7e1c11d40",
      "Description": "Each draw operation comes with overhead.\nThese operations are called draw calls.\nIf you exceed a few thousand draw calls per frame, performance will drop significantly, regardless of how powerful the GPU is."
    },
    {
      "Id": "3e324fc4-e2c1-478f-8b73-1c8101d8bf87",
      "Description": "There are many techniques to render complex scenes with few draw calls.\nCombining many small meshes into a single larger mesh is one of them."
    },
    {
      "Id": "cdcd6cb5-8593-46f4-b36a-a4b42f312a85",
      "Description": "Build the example.\nSome operators already have their parameters set correctly.",
      "Style": "CallToAction"
    }
  ]
}